          ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the second row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1+(3)(9) & -3+(3)(6) & -2+(3)(-7) \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 28 & 15 & -23 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 28+(-1)(-2) & 15+(-1)(4) & -23+(-1)(-3) \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 30 & 11 & -20 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
